WEBVTT


00:00:00.189 --> 00:00:03.488
At least he saw it. I spent
the ovation hiding under the stage.


00:00:03.559 --> 00:00:05.891
No one cares about
the man who disappears.


00:00:05.961 --> 00:00:07.952
They care about the one who comes out.


00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:10.089
I care about the man in the box.


00:00:10.165 --> 00:00:14.465
Thank you. I don't know,
maybe we could switch before the trick.


00:00:14.536 --> 00:00:16.697
I'm the prestige,
and Root's below stage.


00:00:16.772 --> 00:00:19.707
No, the anticipation
of the trick is everything.


00:00:19.775 --> 00:00:22.835
We need your showmanship
to build up the suspense.


00:00:22.911 --> 00:00:26.472
Once Root opens his mouth, it's over.
He can't introduce this trick.


00:00:26.548 --> 00:00:29.278
Of course I can. I'm the Great Danton.


00:00:29.351 --> 00:00:32.946
Root, you bloody fool,
get out of that wardrobe and makeup.


00:00:33.021 --> 00:00:35.683
Anyone could walk in here at any minute.


00:00:35.757 --> 00:00:37.816
Congratulations, all.


00:00:37.893 --> 00:00:41.590
Life is not full of these
moments. We worked hard.


00:00:41.663 --> 00:00:43.324
We need to celebrate properly.


00:00:47.069 --> 00:00:49.537
What's wrong? Is it your wife?


00:00:49.605 --> 00:00:51.903
No, it's the trick.
It isn't good enough.


00:00:51.974 --> 00:00:55.307
Borden's trick is nothing
compared to ours. He has no style.


00:00:55.377 --> 00:00:59.245
He doesn't spend the finale
hiding under the stage.


00:00:59.314 --> 00:01:02.215
- I need to know how he does it.
- Why?


00:01:02.284 --> 00:01:04.775
So I can do it better.


00:01:06.855 --> 00:01:09.323
I need you to go and work for him.


00:01:12.361 --> 00:01:14.090
Work for him? Are you joking?


00:01:15.364 --> 00:01:16.558
You'll be my spy.


00:01:16.632 --> 00:01:18.827
We just got our start.
You want me to leave?


00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:20.994
That's how we advance. Think of it.


00:01:21.069 --> 00:01:24.266
People are excited by Cutter's
version. Imagine what we'd do


00:01:24.339 --> 00:01:28.776
with the real illusion. We'd have the
greatest magic act anyone's ever seen.


00:01:28.844 --> 00:01:32.610
- He knows I work for you.
- Exactly why he'll want to hire you.


00:01:32.681 --> 00:01:35.241
- He'll want my secret.
- Why would he trust me?


00:01:35.317 --> 00:01:38.013
Because you're
gonna tell him the truth.


00:01:40.923 --> 00:01:42.754
Hmm?


00:01:50.299 --> 00:01:51.425
Good girl.


00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.526
[rattling]


00:01:54.603 --> 00:01:58.130
You must be curious to see what
so much money has bought you.


00:01:58.807 --> 00:02:01.708
Fitting you should be here
for her maiden voyage.


00:02:01.777 --> 00:02:03.608
Your hat.


00:02:11.553 --> 00:02:14.147
You might want to stand back.


00:02:16.058 --> 00:02:17.525
[electric zapping]


00:02:29.271 --> 00:02:33.435
[fizzling]


00:02:34.609 --> 00:02:35.735
I don't understand.


00:02:35.811 --> 00:02:38.143
Perhaps it would be best
if you left us to it.


00:02:38.213 --> 00:02:39.840
Is there a problem, Mr. Tesla?


00:02:39.915 --> 00:02:41.940
- No. Come back next week.
- Next week?


00:02:42.017 --> 00:02:44.577
- Next week, it will be fine.
- Tesla!


00:02:44.653 --> 00:02:46.382
Just a little temperamental.


00:02:49.057 --> 00:02:51.048
[door closing]


00:02:52.227 --> 00:02:55.128
- Interesting workshop.
- Yeah, we make do.


00:02:55.197 --> 00:02:57.358
- My name is Olivia...
- I know who you are.


00:02:57.432 --> 00:02:59.093
Here to steal the rest of my show?


00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:01.067
To give your show what it's missing.


00:03:01.136 --> 00:03:04.367
- Yeah, what might that be?
- Me.


00:03:04.439 --> 00:03:08.899
[chuckles] I was just
saying that, wasn't I?


00:03:08.977 --> 00:03:11.275
- A woman's touch.
- I've left Angier.


00:03:11.346 --> 00:03:13.405
- All right.
- I want a job.


00:03:13.482 --> 00:03:14.813
Yeah.


00:03:14.883 --> 00:03:16.714
I know you've no reason to trust me.


00:03:16.785 --> 00:03:18.343
Why wouldn't I trust you?


00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:21.856
You're only the mistress of my
enemy. Why wouldn't I trust you?


00:03:23.525 --> 00:03:25.459
- Mr. Borden.
- Alfred.


00:03:27.896 --> 00:03:29.557
I'm going to tell you the truth.


00:03:29.631 --> 00:03:31.861
Now that is a slippery notion


00:03:31.933 --> 00:03:34.265
in our line of work,
isn't it, Miss Wenscombe?


00:03:36.371 --> 00:03:39.033
I am here because he sent me here.


00:03:39.107 --> 00:03:41.575
He wants me to work for you
and steal your secret.


00:03:41.643 --> 00:03:45.010
What does he need my secret for?
His trick is topnotch.


00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:47.674
He vanishes,
and then he reappears instantly


00:03:47.749 --> 00:03:50.240
on the other side
of the stage, mute, overweight


00:03:50.318 --> 00:03:52.878
and, unless I'm mistaken, very drunk.


00:03:52.954 --> 00:03:56.446
It's astonishing. How does
he do it? And tell me, Olivia,


00:03:56.525 --> 00:03:59.983
does he enjoy taking his bows
under the stage?


00:04:00.062 --> 00:04:03.361
It's killing him. He's obsessed
with discovering your methods.


00:04:03.432 --> 00:04:06.492
He thinks of nothing else,
takes no pleasure in our success.


00:04:06.568 --> 00:04:08.058
And I've had enough.


00:04:08.136 --> 00:04:10.536
There is no future with him.


00:04:11.673 --> 00:04:15.404
He sent me here to steal your secrets,
but I've come to offer you his.


00:04:15.477 --> 00:04:19.379
This is the truth... is it?


00:04:23.919 --> 00:04:26.217
Think you'd better get dressed, sir.


00:04:26.288 --> 00:04:30.315
Root, you're late and more drunk than
usual. Get down below stairs right away.


00:04:30.392 --> 00:04:32.121
No.


00:04:32.194 --> 00:04:35.561
No, we need to have
a little chat, Mr. Cutter.


00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:39.964
We have a problem. Cutter, Borden
is performing right across the street.


00:04:40.035 --> 00:04:43.300
Yeah, we have a bigger problem.


00:04:43.371 --> 00:04:46.363
Root. He's realized
that he can make demands.


00:04:46.441 --> 00:04:48.534
Wha...? He's blackmailing us?


00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:50.578
I was surprised, to tell you the truth.


00:04:50.645 --> 00:04:53.239
It usually takes them
a lot longer to figure it out.


00:04:53.315 --> 00:04:55.875
- How much does he want?
- It makes no difference.


00:04:55.951 --> 00:04:59.409
- We've got to stop doing the trick.
- Stop the trick? Look at this.


00:04:59.488 --> 00:05:05.324
Last week they said you were
the premier stage performer in London.


00:05:05.393 --> 00:05:08.760
Not magician, mind you.
Performer of any kind.


00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:12.061
- What's your point?
- My point is, you've climbed too high


00:05:12.134 --> 00:05:14.568
to get away with
professional embarrassment.


00:05:14.636 --> 00:05:18.003
We don't do any tricks we can't control.


00:05:20.175 --> 00:05:23.474
Just pay him for now. We keep
doing the trick until Borden opens,


00:05:23.545 --> 00:05:25.513
and then we'll phase it out.


00:05:26.414 --> 00:05:27.904
All right.


00:05:30.685 --> 00:05:32.812
<i>[Angier] Cutter was always surprised</i>


00:05:32.888 --> 00:05:34.788
<i>how fast Root turned bad.</i>


00:05:34.856 --> 00:05:39.418
To what do I owe the pleasure
of this rather welcome pint of ale?


00:05:39.494 --> 00:05:42.622
- You're the Great Danton, aren't you?
- Sh, sh, sh, sh, sh.


00:05:42.697 --> 00:05:46.360
Of course I am, but don't advertise it,
because I'll be mobbed with fans.


00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:48.868
<i>[Angier] We paid him enough</i>
<i>to keep him in beers.</i>


00:05:48.937 --> 00:05:51.030
<i>You wouldn't expect him</i>
<i>to rock the boat.</i>


00:05:51.106 --> 00:05:53.700
Many of you may be
familiar with this technique,


00:05:53.775 --> 00:05:57.267
but for those of you
who aren't, do not be alarmed.


00:05:57.345 --> 00:06:00.508
What you're about to see
is considered safe.


00:06:00.582 --> 00:06:04.211
- And who are you?
- I am a humble admirer


00:06:04.286 --> 00:06:06.880
and a fellow practitioner.


00:06:06.955 --> 00:06:09.321
Mmm. Very good.


00:06:13.595 --> 00:06:15.290
[grunts]


00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:21.533
- [Borden] Another one?
- Oh, if you insist.


00:06:21.603 --> 00:06:24.333
- [Borden] Another.
- I'm not performing tonight.


00:06:24.406 --> 00:06:26.431
I'm only doing one show,
but to be frank,


00:06:26.508 --> 00:06:28.840
my people pretty much
run things these days.


00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:30.104
Get up there.


00:06:31.479 --> 00:06:32.537
Get up!


00:06:32.614 --> 00:06:35.378
Your illusion, The Transported Man,


00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:38.044
I'm not claiming to know your methods,


00:06:38.119 --> 00:06:42.317
but I had a similar trick in my act,


00:06:42.390 --> 00:06:45.223
and, uh... [whispering] I used a double.


00:06:45.293 --> 00:06:50.492
- Mm, I see, very good.
- Well, it was, and then it went bad.


00:06:50.565 --> 00:06:53.966
What I didn't count on was that
when I incorporated this bloke


00:06:54.035 --> 00:06:56.128
into my act,


00:06:56.204 --> 00:06:58.195
he had complete power over me.


00:06:59.341 --> 00:07:00.968
Complete power, you say?


00:07:05.413 --> 00:07:07.540
[laughing]


00:07:07.616 --> 00:07:10.176
[applause]


00:07:11.853 --> 00:07:14.447
[grunting]


00:07:16.958 --> 00:07:18.391
Ohh! [laughs]


00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:23.727
Be very careful giving
someone that power over you.


00:07:23.798 --> 00:07:28.132
Huh. Thank you. Um...


00:07:28.203 --> 00:07:31.070
Yes, thank you for the warning.


00:07:31.139 --> 00:07:33.835
Hmm. Cheers.


00:07:35.277 --> 00:07:37.404
I cannot claim
this next feat as illusion.


00:07:37.479 --> 00:07:40.846
What you're about to see
is considered safe.


00:07:45.153 --> 00:07:46.848
Ahh!


00:07:49.557 --> 00:07:52.651
[moaning]


00:08:00.335 --> 00:08:03.031
[crowd laughing]


00:08:03.104 --> 00:08:06.665
[applause]


00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:17.784
[chuckling]


00:08:17.852 --> 00:08:19.012
[laughing, applause]


00:08:19.087 --> 00:08:24.047
Oh! The Great Danton.


00:08:30.265 --> 00:08:32.130
I apologize.


00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:35.966
There simply is too much magic...


00:08:36.037 --> 00:08:38.801
...for my stage at The Pantages


00:08:38.873 --> 00:08:41.034
across the street.


00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:48.015
Pardon my intrusion.


00:08:50.085 --> 00:08:54.488
And go easy on the poor chap.
He does try so very hard.


00:08:54.556 --> 00:08:57.286
[all laughing, applauding]


00:08:57.359 --> 00:08:59.793
I don't know how Borden found him.


00:08:59.861 --> 00:09:01.761
Kept him under wraps. I was careful.


00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:03.491
Yeah, well, he did.


00:09:04.666 --> 00:09:06.657
Do you think it was her?


00:09:12.907 --> 00:09:15.876
You weren't expecting me?


00:09:15.944 --> 00:09:18.674
I expected you sooner.
Your message said afternoon.


00:09:18.747 --> 00:09:21.011
It takes a bit for me
to get around these days.


00:09:21.082 --> 00:09:25.143
He's taken everything from me.
My wife, my career,


00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:27.085
- now you.
- You sent me.


00:09:27.155 --> 00:09:30.215
I sent you to steal his secret,
not to improve his act.


00:09:30.291 --> 00:09:31.849
- It's my job.
- Or fall in love!


00:09:31.926 --> 00:09:34.690
- I did everything you asked!
- Yes? Yes?


00:09:34.763 --> 00:09:37.254
- How does he do it?
- Cutter was right, a double.


00:09:37.332 --> 00:09:39.562
- 'Course he said that.
- He didn't say it.


00:09:39.634 --> 00:09:43.070
I've seen things, makeup, glasses, wigs.
We don't use for the show.


00:09:43.138 --> 00:09:45.868
- I've seen it hidden backstage.
- Misdirection.


00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:48.636
He leaves them lying
around to make you think that.


00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:50.575
He doesn't know when I'm looking.


00:09:50.645 --> 00:09:53.876
All the time, Olivia! That's who he is!


00:09:53.948 --> 00:09:55.210
That's what it takes!


00:09:55.283 --> 00:09:57.717
He lives his act, don't you see?


00:09:59.754 --> 00:10:03.121
Just because you're sleeping
with him doesn't mean he trusts you.


00:10:03.191 --> 00:10:05.591
You think you can see
everything, don't you?


00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:08.493
The Great Danton is a blind fool.


00:10:08.563 --> 00:10:09.962
His notebook.


00:10:11.332 --> 00:10:13.596
You stole it?


00:10:13.668 --> 00:10:15.465
I borrowed it for tonight.


00:10:15.537 --> 00:10:17.732
I thought you could translate
some of it...


00:10:17.806 --> 00:10:21.867
I can't. No one can. It's a cipher.


00:10:21.943 --> 00:10:25.379
Even with the keyword,
it will take months to decode.


00:10:25.447 --> 00:10:28.348
- And without the keyword?
- Perhaps never.


00:10:28.416 --> 00:10:30.043
- We'll see.
- We will not see.


00:10:30.118 --> 00:10:33.053
If I don't get that back by
tomorrow he'll know I took it.


00:10:33.121 --> 00:10:35.419
- Leave him.
- I can't. He knows where I live.


00:10:36.758 --> 00:10:41.559
This is his diary, Olivia. All of his
secrets are right here in my hands.


00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:43.822
It won't bring your wife back.


00:10:43.898 --> 00:10:46.594
I don't care about my wife.
I care about his secret.


00:10:53.975 --> 00:10:56.876
[sighs, grunts]


00:10:59.848 --> 00:11:02.578
Look, I'll, um...


00:11:02.650 --> 00:11:04.982
I'll go to his workshop
and stage a break-in.


00:11:05.053 --> 00:11:08.250
- He'll know you took it.
- Yes, me. Not you.


00:11:09.357 --> 00:11:11.348
Understand?


00:11:19.801 --> 00:11:20.790
Robert.


00:11:23.204 --> 00:11:26.002
I have fallen in love with him.


00:11:26.908 --> 00:11:29.376
Then I know how hard
this has been for you.


00:11:37.919 --> 00:11:39.409
Notebook?


00:11:42.056 --> 00:11:44.047
Then he's just getting started.


00:11:44.192 --> 00:11:46.285
[clapping]


00:11:46.361 --> 00:11:50.388
- [drumroll]
- [cymbal crashes]


00:11:50.465 --> 00:11:53.127
[electrical zapping]


00:12:00.875 --> 00:12:03.275
[applause]


00:12:13.288 --> 00:12:14.755
[all] Professor!


00:12:14.822 --> 00:12:16.312
Good evening.


00:12:16.391 --> 00:12:18.450
[chattering]


00:12:21.195 --> 00:12:22.822
I'm walking tonight.


00:12:22.897 --> 00:12:25.457
Let him come. I don't care.


00:12:25.533 --> 00:12:28.229
[all] Professor! Professor!


00:12:55.863 --> 00:12:57.854
[man yells]


00:13:04.472 --> 00:13:07.737
[heart beating]


00:13:30.732 --> 00:13:32.859
[man gagging, coughing]


00:13:50.618 --> 00:13:52.051
- [gunshot]
- Ahh!


00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:54.680
- You all right?
- I'm alive.


00:13:54.756 --> 00:13:56.849
Saves me cutting you an air hole.


00:14:10.938 --> 00:14:13.498
- I'm impressed.
- Why is that?


00:14:13.574 --> 00:14:16.543
You're finally getting your hands dirty.


00:14:16.611 --> 00:14:19.512
It's what a good trick costs, Angier.


00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:22.378
Risk, sacrifice.


00:14:22.450 --> 00:14:24.941
The sacrifice, I'm afraid,
is all gonna be yours,


00:14:25.019 --> 00:14:26.646
unless you give me what I want.


00:14:28.022 --> 00:14:30.149
- Which is?
- Your secret.


00:14:30.224 --> 00:14:31.623
My secret?


00:14:31.693 --> 00:14:34.821
Your method for The Transported Man.


00:14:34.896 --> 00:14:37.729
Fallon wouldn't tell me.
He doesn't talk at all.


00:14:37.799 --> 00:14:41.291
- You have my notebook.
- Useless without the keyword.


00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:46.331
Write down your method,
Mr. Borden, describe it in full.


00:14:59.454 --> 00:15:01.820
I want the whole method,
not the keyword.


00:15:01.889 --> 00:15:04.289
I don't know if your secret's
in your notebook.


00:15:04.358 --> 00:15:06.826
The keyword is the method.


00:15:10.832 --> 00:15:12.129
Where's my <i>ingénieur</i>?


00:15:19.273 --> 00:15:21.901
- Alive?
- How fast can you dig?


00:15:24.378 --> 00:15:27.404
Fallon, you hear me? Fallon!


00:15:28.716 --> 00:15:31.378
- [Angier] How's the arm?
- Still attached.


00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:34.378
Did you find your answer?


00:15:34.455 --> 00:15:38.221
Our answer, Cutter. I haven't
looked yet. I wanted you to share this.


00:15:38.292 --> 00:15:40.726
I already know how he does it, Robert.


00:15:40.795 --> 00:15:43.889
Same way he always has,
the same way as we do.


00:15:43.965 --> 00:15:46.433
It's just that you want something more.


00:15:46.501 --> 00:15:49.265
Well, let's find out then, shall we?


00:15:53.574 --> 00:15:55.007
What does it mean?


00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.318
It means, Cutter, we have
a journey ahead of us.


00:16:05.386 --> 00:16:08.253
- To America.
- Robert?


00:16:08.322 --> 00:16:11.291
Listen to me.


00:16:11.359 --> 00:16:14.817
Obsession is a young man's game.


00:16:14.896 --> 00:16:16.420
Come on.


00:16:16.497 --> 00:16:18.965
I can't follow you any further in it.


00:16:20.034 --> 00:16:21.968
I can't, I'm sorry.


00:16:26.073 --> 00:16:27.768
Then the rest is up to me.


00:16:29.844 --> 00:16:31.368
I'm sorry.


00:16:36.684 --> 00:16:40.279
Good evening. Hello, darling. [laughs]


00:16:40.354 --> 00:16:41.844
Champagne, your finest.


00:16:41.923 --> 00:16:44.619
I didn't know we were going
to be joined for dinner.


00:16:44.692 --> 00:16:46.990
Absolutely, we are celebrating.


00:16:47.061 --> 00:16:48.756
Miss Wenscombe, Mr. Fallon.


00:16:49.764 --> 00:16:52.631
- What are we celebrating?
- We've hit upon a new trick.


00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:54.759
- Haven't we?
- What trick, Freddie?


00:16:54.836 --> 00:16:56.861
Yes, Freddie, what trick?


00:16:56.938 --> 00:17:01.341
I am going to bury
myself alive every night,


00:17:01.409 --> 00:17:05.277
and then someone will come along
and dig me up. Wonderful.


00:17:05.346 --> 00:17:08.440
- I think he's had quite enough...
- No, pour the champagne.


00:17:08.516 --> 00:17:12.213
Pour the... Sarah, don't talk to me
like that. I'm not a bloody child.


00:17:12.286 --> 00:17:15.483
- Perhaps it would be better...
- Mr. Fallon, escort her home.


00:17:15.556 --> 00:17:18.389
- My husband's being a bore.
- Oh, please.


00:17:18.459 --> 00:17:22.259
- I see no reason you should suffer.
- Don't ruin this evening.


00:17:24.665 --> 00:17:27.566
Good night, Mrs. Borden.
Good night, Freddie.


00:17:32.006 --> 00:17:34.304
- Freddie?
- That's my name.


00:17:34.375 --> 00:17:37.742
- Not at home.
- I'm not always at home, am I?


00:17:39.547 --> 00:17:42.209
Couldn't you have at least
taken off the beard?


00:17:42.283 --> 00:17:46.447
Sarah, I just came from
the bloody theater just now.


00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:49.580
All right? I'm out in public.
Everybody else loves it.


00:17:49.657 --> 00:17:51.591
Why are you being like this?


00:17:51.659 --> 00:17:54.560
I had a terrible ordeal today.


00:17:54.629 --> 00:17:58.395
I thought that
something very precious...


00:17:59.567 --> 00:18:01.501
...had been lost to me.


00:18:01.569 --> 00:18:04.697
So I just wanted
to celebrate just a little.


00:18:04.772 --> 00:18:08.230
All right, what? What did you lose?


00:18:13.381 --> 00:18:14.939
I see, more secrets.


00:18:15.883 --> 00:18:19.046
Sarah, secrets are my life.


00:18:20.988 --> 00:18:24.253
- Our life.
- No, Alfred, stop, this isn't you.


00:18:24.325 --> 00:18:26.793
Stop performing.


00:18:28.796 --> 00:18:30.957
[shudders]


00:18:50.952 --> 00:18:53.443
I thought I had the place to myself.


00:18:53.521 --> 00:18:56.820
Unexpected guests, not very polite.


00:18:56.891 --> 00:18:58.722
A lot of questions.


00:18:58.793 --> 00:19:01.591
At first, I thought they
worked for the government.


00:19:01.662 --> 00:19:05.325
- No?
- Worse, they work for Thomas Edison.


00:19:07.301 --> 00:19:09.792
<i>[Borden] Today, a most</i>
<i>curious development.</i>


00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:12.930
<i>His assistant came to us</i>
<i>with a proposition.</i>


00:19:14.575 --> 00:19:17.976
<i>Obviously, Angier has sent her</i>
<i>and told her to admit as much.</i>


00:19:18.045 --> 00:19:20.843
Does he enjoy taking
his bows under the stage?


00:19:20.915 --> 00:19:24.681
He sent me here to steal your secrets,
but I've come to offer you his.


00:19:24.752 --> 00:19:27.721
This is the truth...


00:19:27.788 --> 00:19:28.777
...is it?


00:19:36.831 --> 00:19:40.289
No, that's what he told
me to tell you. The truth...


00:19:40.368 --> 00:19:44.202
...is that I loved him and I stood by
him and he sent me to you,


00:19:44.271 --> 00:19:47.798
like he would send a stagehand
to pick up his shirts.


00:19:47.875 --> 00:19:50.673
I hate him for that.


00:19:50.745 --> 00:19:53.976
I could spot Angier's methods
from the back of the theater.


00:19:55.683 --> 00:19:57.947
So, what could you
possibly have to offer me?


00:19:58.019 --> 00:19:59.646
You may know his tricks,


00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:02.780
but you can't understand why
no one sees yours are better.


00:20:02.857 --> 00:20:05.417
You hide this.
I had to look very closely


00:20:05.493 --> 00:20:07.825
to spot it
during The Transported Man,


00:20:07.895 --> 00:20:10.728
but this makes you unique.


00:20:10.798 --> 00:20:12.823
It shows you aren't using a double.


00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:15.391
You mustn't hide it.
You must display it proudly.


00:20:15.469 --> 00:20:20.236
I'm sure it takes great skill
to perform illusions with one good hand.


00:20:20.307 --> 00:20:22.070
Yeah, it does.


00:20:23.844 --> 00:20:27.007
So let people know.


00:20:27.081 --> 00:20:30.573
You can be so much more than
he is and I can show you how.


00:20:32.286 --> 00:20:34.880
<i>[Borden] I think</i>
<i>she's telling the truth.</i>


00:20:34.955 --> 00:20:37.082
<i>I think we cannot trust her.</i>


00:20:40.628 --> 00:20:43.096
<i>But I love her. I need her.</i>


00:20:44.298 --> 00:20:47.631
<i>To open myself to such a relationship,</i>


00:20:47.701 --> 00:20:51.535
<i>to the dangers of such an affair,</i>


00:20:51.605 --> 00:20:56.406
<i>I need assurances of fidelity, of love.</i>


00:20:57.445 --> 00:20:59.037
<i>But how to be sure?</i>


00:21:01.248 --> 00:21:05.582
<i>I know a way. It's the only</i>
<i>way to know her mind.</i>


00:21:05.653 --> 00:21:07.484
How could he send you away?


00:21:09.356 --> 00:21:12.450
<i>[Borden] She must help me</i>
<i>rid ourselves of Angier.</i>


00:21:19.066 --> 00:21:22.058
<i>Today, my mistress</i>
<i>proves her truthfulness.</i>


00:21:22.136 --> 00:21:23.865
<i>Not to me, you understand.</i>


00:21:23.938 --> 00:21:26.566
<i>I've been</i>
<i>convinced since she led me to Root.</i>


00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:30.167
<i>Today, Olivia proves her love for me</i>


00:21:30.244 --> 00:21:32.712
<i>to you, Angier.</i>


00:21:32.780 --> 00:21:37.183
<i>Yes, Angier, she gave you</i>
<i>this notebook at my request.</i>


00:21:37.251 --> 00:21:40.687
<i>And yes, "Tesla" is merely</i>
<i>the key to my dairy,</i>


00:21:40.754 --> 00:21:43.552
<i>not to my trick.</i>
<i>You really think I'd part</i>


00:21:43.624 --> 00:21:46.752
<i>with my secret so easily after so much?</i>


00:21:46.827 --> 00:21:48.488
<i>Goodbye, Angier.</i>


00:21:48.562 --> 00:21:50.928
<i>May you find solace</i>
<i>for your forward ambition</i>


00:21:50.998 --> 00:21:52.795
<i>back in your American home.</i>


00:22:02.309 --> 00:22:03.936
Tesla!


00:22:05.880 --> 00:22:08.280
Tesla! Alley!


00:22:09.483 --> 00:22:10.472
Alley!


00:22:10.551 --> 00:22:13.145
Tesla never made a machine
like the one I asked for.


00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:16.018
- I never said he had.
- You let me believe that he had.


00:22:16.090 --> 00:22:18.786
You stole my money because
your funding was cut off.


00:22:18.859 --> 00:22:21.760
You've been shooting
sparks in my top hat,


00:22:21.829 --> 00:22:25.321
laughing at me all along,
while using my money to stave off ruin.


00:22:26.167 --> 00:22:28.294
- I have seen Edison's men.
- Where?


00:22:28.369 --> 00:22:30.860
In the hotel, I have a mind
to bring them up here.


00:22:30.938 --> 00:22:33.634
That would be unwise, Mr. Angier.


00:22:33.707 --> 00:22:36.835
It is true that you are
our last remaining financier,


00:22:36.911 --> 00:22:38.776
but we have not stolen your money.


00:22:38.846 --> 00:22:40.313
This is my cat.


00:22:40.381 --> 00:22:43.441
When I told you I could make you
a machine, I spoke a truth.


00:22:43.517 --> 00:22:44.609
Why isn't it working?


00:22:44.685 --> 00:22:47.017
Because exact science, Mr. Angier,


00:22:47.087 --> 00:22:48.486
is not an exact science.


00:22:48.556 --> 00:22:51.719
The machine simply
does not operate as expected.


00:22:51.792 --> 00:22:55.819
- It requires further examination.
- So where did my top hat go?


00:22:55.896 --> 00:22:56.954
Nowhere.


00:22:57.031 --> 00:22:59.829
We tried the damn thing a dozen times.


00:22:59.900 --> 00:23:01.527
The hat went nowhere.


00:23:01.602 --> 00:23:03.502
We need to try different material.


00:23:03.571 --> 00:23:05.732
It may provoke a different result.


00:23:06.273 --> 00:23:08.298
[meowing]


00:23:08.375 --> 00:23:09.933
Great.


00:23:17.084 --> 00:23:21.043
You are responsible for whatever
happens to this animal, doctor.


00:23:25.559 --> 00:23:26.685
[meows]


00:23:26.760 --> 00:23:29.251
[electrical zapping]


00:23:39.740 --> 00:23:42.504
[sighs]


00:23:42.576 --> 00:23:45.204
I hope whatever you were
really doing with my money


00:23:45.279 --> 00:23:47.713
was more worthwhile, Mr. Tesla.


00:24:00.027 --> 00:24:02.120
[meowing]


00:24:02.196 --> 00:24:05.029
[cats screeching]


00:24:15.209 --> 00:24:18.440
[screeching continues]


00:24:18.512 --> 00:24:20.742
[hissing]


00:24:43.637 --> 00:24:44.626
Alley!


00:24:47.708 --> 00:24:49.437
So the machine was working?


00:24:49.510 --> 00:24:53.139
I never checked the calibration,
'cause the hat never moved.


00:24:53.213 --> 00:24:56.080
These things never quite
work as you expect them to.


00:24:56.150 --> 00:24:58.641
That's one of the principal
beauties of science.


00:24:58.719 --> 00:25:02.177
I'll need a couple of weeks to iron out
the problems with the machine.


00:25:02.256 --> 00:25:04.315
We'll send word when it's ready.


00:25:06.527 --> 00:25:09.496
Don't forget your hat.


00:25:09.563 --> 00:25:13.294
- Well, which one is mine?
- They are all your hats.


00:25:19.239 --> 00:25:22.231
You look so pretty
in this new dress of yours.


00:25:22.309 --> 00:25:26.143
- Are we going to the zoo?
- No, Daddy has some errands to run.


00:25:26.213 --> 00:25:28.443
- But you promised.
- I promised, did I?


00:25:28.515 --> 00:25:30.813
Then go to the zoo, we shall.


00:25:30.884 --> 00:25:34.342
Daddy will go run his errands,
and I'll be back before you know it.


00:25:34.421 --> 00:25:38.152
So you go get ready. We'll go
see those chimpanzees. [hoots]


00:25:41.161 --> 00:25:44.562
Sarah... what are you doing?


00:25:48.235 --> 00:25:51.227
Each of us have our vices.


00:25:54.341 --> 00:25:56.809
Sarah, whatever you may think...


00:25:58.379 --> 00:26:02.008
...your only competition
for my affections is our little girl.


00:26:02.082 --> 00:26:05.051
I love you. I will always love you


00:26:05.119 --> 00:26:06.552
and you alone.


00:26:08.422 --> 00:26:12.222
- You mean it today.
- Absolutely.


00:26:12.292 --> 00:26:16.126
Which makes it so much
harder when you don't.


00:26:25.472 --> 00:26:28.270
More shopping. She does
love the smell of money.


00:26:28.342 --> 00:26:32.642
The little lady wants to go to the zoo,
so I thought you could take her, yeah?


00:26:32.713 --> 00:26:35.079
I mean, I can do it tomorrow, if not.


00:26:35.149 --> 00:26:38.448
And, uh... Sarah,


00:26:38.519 --> 00:26:40.646
she knows.


00:26:40.721 --> 00:26:44.885
Uh, at least she knows
that something is not right,


00:26:44.958 --> 00:26:47.859
so if you can just do
whatever you can to help me.


00:26:47.928 --> 00:26:52.490
Talk to her, just
convince her that I do love her.


00:27:03.143 --> 00:27:05.111
What is it, Freddie?


00:27:05.179 --> 00:27:07.477
Listen, don't call me that, please.


00:27:07.548 --> 00:27:11.416
It's nothing. It's just that
sometimes it seems wrong.


00:27:11.485 --> 00:27:13.976
I told you, when you're
with me, you're with me.


00:27:14.054 --> 00:27:17.080
Leave your family at home
where they belong.


00:27:17.157 --> 00:27:20.422
I'm trying. I'm trying, Olivia.


00:27:20.494 --> 00:27:22.860
- I'll get dressed.
- Yeah.


00:27:24.364 --> 00:27:27.390
I saw Fallon hanging around again.


00:27:27.468 --> 00:27:29.936
There's something about
that man I don't trust.


00:27:30.003 --> 00:27:33.063
You trust me? Then trust Fallon.


00:27:33.140 --> 00:27:35.802
He protects the things
that I care about.


00:27:35.876 --> 00:27:38.868
[engine sputters]


00:28:14.047 --> 00:28:16.538
We're sorry to see you go, Mr. Angier.


00:28:16.617 --> 00:28:19.177
We were sorry to see
Mr. Tesla leave, as well.


00:28:19.253 --> 00:28:21.346
He's very good to Colorado Springs.


00:28:21.421 --> 00:28:24.083
Mr. Angier,


00:28:24.157 --> 00:28:27.786
I didn't think it was necessary
to tell Edison's men about the box.


00:28:27.861 --> 00:28:29.522
What box?


00:28:54.855 --> 00:28:58.256
<i>[Tesla] I apologize for leaving</i>
<i>without saying goodbye.</i>


00:28:58.325 --> 00:29:03.558
<i>But I seem to have outstayed</i>
<i>my welcome in Colorado.</i>


00:29:03.630 --> 00:29:08.124
<i>The truly extraordinary is not</i>
<i>permitted in science and industry.</i>


00:29:08.201 --> 00:29:10.999
<i>Perhaps you'll find</i>
<i>more luck in your field,</i>


00:29:11.071 --> 00:29:13.733
<i>where people are happy to be mystified.</i>


00:29:13.807 --> 00:29:17.766
<i>You will find what you</i>
<i>are looking for in this box.</i>


00:29:17.844 --> 00:29:22.281
<i>Alley has written you</i>
<i>a thorough set of instructions.</i>


00:29:22.349 --> 00:29:27.082
<i>I add only one suggestion</i>
<i>on using the machine.</i>


00:29:27.154 --> 00:29:29.122
<i>Destroy it.</i>


00:29:29.189 --> 00:29:32.488
<i>Drop it to the bottom</i>
<i>of the deepest ocean.</i>


00:29:32.559 --> 00:29:35.960
<i>Such a thing will bring you only misery.</i>


00:29:39.833 --> 00:29:43.462
<i>[Angier] Tesla's warning is</i>
<i>as unheeded as he knew it would be.</i>


00:29:43.537 --> 00:29:47.098
<i>Today I tested the machine.</i>
<i>Taking precautions in case</i>


00:29:47.174 --> 00:29:50.143
<i>Tesla hadn't ironed out</i>
<i>the kinks in its operation.</i>


00:29:50.210 --> 00:29:52.007
<i>But if it went wrong,</i>


00:29:52.079 --> 00:29:54.240
<i>I would not want to live</i>
<i>like that for long.</i>


00:29:56.984 --> 00:29:58.576
[electrical zapping]


00:30:13.700 --> 00:30:17.830
<i>[Angier] But here at the turn,</i>
<i>I must leave you, Borden.</i>


00:30:17.904 --> 00:30:20.134
<i>Yes, you, Borden,</i>


00:30:20.207 --> 00:30:22.573
<i>sitting there in your cell,</i>


00:30:22.643 --> 00:30:26.670
<i>reading my diary, awaiting your death,</i>


00:30:26.747 --> 00:30:28.738
<i>for my murder.</i>


00:30:34.087 --> 00:30:37.386
Angier's journal, that gesture
of good faith, that's a fake.


00:30:37.457 --> 00:30:38.754
I assure you, it's not.


00:30:38.825 --> 00:30:41.760
The provenance of the journal
is clear and under no doubt.


00:30:41.828 --> 00:30:46.322
And it's written in Angier's own hand,
for which we have numerous examples.


00:30:48.201 --> 00:30:50.101
It don't matter.


00:30:52.039 --> 00:30:54.064
So my tricks.


00:30:57.310 --> 00:31:00.768
- All of them.
- Including The Transported Man?


00:31:02.215 --> 00:31:05.412
- Lord Caldlow will be very pleased.
- No, he won't.


00:31:05.485 --> 00:31:07.851
They're not complete.


00:31:07.921 --> 00:31:10.651
It's just the pledge
and the turn for each.


00:31:10.724 --> 00:31:14.785
Without the prestige for these
tricks, these are worthless.


00:31:14.861 --> 00:31:16.886
Yeah.


00:31:16.963 --> 00:31:20.490
You get the rest of it...
when you bring my daughter here.


00:31:23.236 --> 00:31:25.466
I want to say goodbye.


00:31:27.207 --> 00:31:30.370
[Sarah] We have to go through it now.
We have to go through it now.


00:31:30.444 --> 00:31:32.810
Now, listen to me, deny it all you want.


00:31:32.879 --> 00:31:35.245
Olivia means nothing.


00:31:35.315 --> 00:31:37.112
- Olivia?
- I need an assistant.


00:31:37.184 --> 00:31:40.017
- I'll go to her, I'll tell her.
- You'll tell her what?


00:31:40.087 --> 00:31:42.146
I know what you really are, Alfred.


00:31:44.257 --> 00:31:46.020
- I know.
- Sarah, Sarah, Sarah.


00:31:46.093 --> 00:31:48.721
- I can't keep it in.
- You can't talk like this.


00:31:48.795 --> 00:31:51.320
- No. No.
- Sarah, shut up! Sarah, shut up!


00:31:51.398 --> 00:31:55.528
I don't want to hear it anymore.
You can't talk like this.


00:31:58.138 --> 00:32:01.539
[Sarah] You can't hide it anymore,
because I know, Alfred, I know.


00:32:01.608 --> 00:32:05.044
I know what you really are, Alfred.


00:32:05.112 --> 00:32:07.910
I can't live like this.


00:32:07.981 --> 00:32:10.108
Oh, well, you think
I can live like this?


00:32:10.183 --> 00:32:13.346
You think I bloody enjoy
living like this?


00:32:13.420 --> 00:32:17.823
We have this beautiful house,
lovely little girl, we're married.


00:32:17.891 --> 00:32:19.552
What is so wrong with your life?


00:32:19.626 --> 00:32:22.220
Alfred, I can't live like this!


00:32:22.295 --> 00:32:24.661
Well, what do you want from me?


00:32:28.001 --> 00:32:31.698
I... I want...


00:32:31.772 --> 00:32:34.832
I want you to be... honest with me.


00:32:37.577 --> 00:32:40.045
No tricks.


00:32:40.113 --> 00:32:42.206
No lies.


00:32:42.282 --> 00:32:46.082
And no secrets.


00:32:52.359 --> 00:32:55.692
Do you... do you love me?


00:32:58.765 --> 00:33:00.392
Not today.


00:33:02.536 --> 00:33:03.594
No.


00:33:08.141 --> 00:33:10.974
[birds chirping]


00:33:41.107 --> 00:33:43.905
- [crashing]
- [birds squawking]


00:34:14.774 --> 00:34:17.709
[seagulls calling]


00:34:28.722 --> 00:34:30.952
[birds fluttering]


00:34:41.268 --> 00:34:42.292
Who's there?


00:34:45.438 --> 00:34:47.531
I'm looking for an old friend.


00:34:47.607 --> 00:34:50.542
I heard about a booking,
nice little theater,


00:34:50.610 --> 00:34:53.044
- good up-and-coming magician.
- You're back.


00:34:53.113 --> 00:34:54.705
It's good to see you, John.


00:34:55.482 --> 00:34:58.212
Good rehearsal space.


00:34:58.285 --> 00:35:01.049
Blind stagehands, I like it. [laughs]


00:35:01.121 --> 00:35:03.783
You always had a good eye for publicity.


00:35:03.857 --> 00:35:05.188
I need your help, John.


00:35:05.258 --> 00:35:08.056
It's my last show. A limited engagement.


00:35:08.128 --> 00:35:09.755
Your last show?


00:35:09.829 --> 00:35:13.959
A wise man once told me obsession
was a young man's game.


00:35:14.034 --> 00:35:17.595
I'm almost done. There's one thing left.


00:35:18.605 --> 00:35:21.130
The Real Transported Man.


00:35:22.943 --> 00:35:24.934
You want to design a show around it?


00:35:25.011 --> 00:35:27.878
I don't want you backstage
I need you in front managing.


00:35:27.948 --> 00:35:30.610
Call in any favors
or connections you have left


00:35:30.684 --> 00:35:32.151
to get us the right booking.


00:35:32.218 --> 00:35:34.311
What sort of booking you after?


00:35:34.387 --> 00:35:36.787
The sort that Borden can't ignore.


00:35:43.163 --> 00:35:46.394
Oh, what an honor it is
to see you again, sir.


00:35:46.466 --> 00:35:50.425
You told me you only wanted to show me
one trick that'd pique my interest.


00:35:50.503 --> 00:35:53.666
- It's a very clever trick.
- Pleased to meet you, Mr. Ackerman.


00:35:53.740 --> 00:35:56.607
Likewise, I'm sure.
Let's get on, shall we?


00:36:00.246 --> 00:36:02.009
Turn it on, gentlemen.


00:36:07.253 --> 00:36:08.379
Very pretty.


00:36:19.432 --> 00:36:23.095
That's it, Cutter? He simply disappears?


00:36:23.169 --> 00:36:25.535
That's not a trick. He has to come back.


00:36:25.605 --> 00:36:27.766
- There has to be a...
- [Angier] A prestige?


00:36:27.841 --> 00:36:28.830
Exactly.


00:36:31.845 --> 00:36:34.507
Pardon me.


00:36:34.581 --> 00:36:37.846
It's very rare to see...


00:36:37.917 --> 00:36:39.384
...real magic.


00:36:40.887 --> 00:36:42.582
It's been many years since...


00:36:42.655 --> 00:36:44.384
Are you interested in helping us?


00:36:46.459 --> 00:36:50.190
Yes... but you'll have
to dress it up a little.


00:36:52.465 --> 00:36:54.126
Disguise it.


00:36:55.802 --> 00:36:58.293
Give them enough reason to doubt it.


00:36:59.105 --> 00:37:02.336
You haven't spoken
about her, Freddie, not once.


00:37:02.409 --> 00:37:06.106
Why would I talk about her to you, hm?


00:37:06.179 --> 00:37:10.047
Because she was a part of
your life and now she's gone.


00:37:13.019 --> 00:37:17.513
You know, the day before she killed
herself she said she wanted to meet me.


00:37:17.590 --> 00:37:20.525
That she had something
to tell me about you.


00:37:20.593 --> 00:37:24.188
I was such a coward,
I couldn't bring myself to face her.


00:37:24.264 --> 00:37:25.754
But...


00:37:26.966 --> 00:37:29.230
...what would she have said?


00:37:29.302 --> 00:37:32.396
You want to know the truth about me?


00:37:33.673 --> 00:37:36.164
The truth is that...


00:37:38.344 --> 00:37:40.335
...I never loved Sarah.


00:37:41.548 --> 00:37:43.038
I never loved her.


00:37:43.116 --> 00:37:45.346
You married her,
you had a child with her.


00:37:45.418 --> 00:37:48.512
Yes. Part of me. Part of me did, but...


00:37:48.588 --> 00:37:50.522
...the other part didn't.


00:37:50.590 --> 00:37:54.822
The part that found you,
the part that's sitting here right now.


00:37:54.894 --> 00:37:57.954
I love you. No, Olivia, I love you.


00:37:58.031 --> 00:37:59.999
That's the truth.


00:38:00.066 --> 00:38:02.466
That is the truth that matters.


00:38:02.535 --> 00:38:06.938
You could be in some other restaurant
with some other woman right now,


00:38:07.006 --> 00:38:08.598
talking about me that way.


00:38:08.675 --> 00:38:10.802
- No.
- Yes.


00:38:14.247 --> 00:38:17.978
It's inhuman to be so cold.


00:38:23.656 --> 00:38:24.918
He's back.


00:38:25.825 --> 00:38:29.090
After two years, he's got a new trick.


00:38:29.162 --> 00:38:31.824
They're saying it's
the best London's ever seen.


00:38:34.033 --> 00:38:36.501
You should see the look
on your face, Professor.


00:38:38.371 --> 00:38:40.305
You should go to him.


00:38:40.373 --> 00:38:42.898
You two deserve each other.


00:38:47.881 --> 00:38:51.817
But I'm afraid I'm booked. The Moscow
Ballet plays through next year.


00:38:51.885 --> 00:38:56.447
Then get rid of them. There will be
100 performances, no more, no less.


00:38:56.523 --> 00:38:59.014
Five performances a week, no matinees.


00:39:00.827 --> 00:39:03.853
That's what you'll
charge for each ticket. Good day.


00:39:07.233 --> 00:39:11.499
[applause]


00:39:11.571 --> 00:39:15.007
[footsteps on stage]


00:39:26.586 --> 00:39:31.216
Ladies and gentlemen, my first trick of
the evening involves considerable risk.


00:39:32.458 --> 00:39:33.823
Anyone in the audience


00:39:33.893 --> 00:39:36.726
who would be irrevocably
damaged by seeing a man drown


00:39:36.796 --> 00:39:38.388
should leave now.


00:39:38.464 --> 00:39:41.262
When I tell you the lady
who taught me this illusion


00:39:41.334 --> 00:39:43.325
actually died performing it,


00:39:43.403 --> 00:39:46.702
you'll understand the seriousness
of the dangers involved.


00:39:48.875 --> 00:39:51.275
- Let's begin.
- [applause]


00:40:00.987 --> 00:40:03.615
In my travels, I have seen the future.


00:40:05.425 --> 00:40:09.020
And it is a strange future, indeed.


00:40:09.095 --> 00:40:11.256
The world, ladies and gentlemen,


00:40:11.331 --> 00:40:13.629
is on the brink of new


00:40:13.700 --> 00:40:15.429
and terrifying possibilities.


00:40:15.501 --> 00:40:17.492
[taps cane]


00:40:24.510 --> 00:40:28.742
[applause]


00:40:35.922 --> 00:40:39.380
What you're about to witness
is not magic.


00:40:40.560 --> 00:40:41.959
It's purely science.


00:40:42.028 --> 00:40:44.462
I'd like to invite you
to come up on stage now


00:40:44.530 --> 00:40:47.522
so that you can examine
the machine for yourselves.


00:41:03.483 --> 00:41:05.815
[electrical zapping]


00:41:38.084 --> 00:41:40.814
[crowd murmuring, gasping]


00:41:40.887 --> 00:41:42.752
[applause]


00:41:42.822 --> 00:41:44.653
Man's reach


00:41:44.724 --> 00:41:47.852
exceeds his imagination.


00:41:47.927 --> 00:41:51.522
[applause, cheering]


00:41:59.138 --> 00:42:00.503
Bravo!


00:42:08.548 --> 00:42:11.278
One hundred performances. Why?


00:42:11.351 --> 00:42:12.909
Does his method dictate that?


00:42:12.985 --> 00:42:14.885
Is it a publicity move? What is it?


00:42:14.954 --> 00:42:17.320
He's a no-talent magician,
and they call him


00:42:17.390 --> 00:42:19.790
the bloody best in England. Why?


00:42:19.859 --> 00:42:22.623
Fifty yards in a second! In a second!


00:42:22.695 --> 00:42:25.789
And all that we know
is he uses a trap door.


00:42:25.865 --> 00:42:30.131
Brilliant! What is going on
under that stage? Huh?!


00:42:30.203 --> 00:42:32.637
Why can't you out-think him?


00:42:47.754 --> 00:42:52.953
They do this every night,
after each performance. Yeah?


00:42:53.025 --> 00:42:55.516
[sighs]


00:43:19.252 --> 00:43:20.583
[Borden] Huh.


00:43:21.454 --> 00:43:24.423
- [crumpling paper]
- We're done.


00:43:25.725 --> 00:43:27.283
All right?


00:43:28.594 --> 00:43:30.357
Let him have his trick.


00:43:30.430 --> 00:43:32.921
I don't need his secret.


00:43:32.999 --> 00:43:34.489
So...


00:43:36.002 --> 00:43:38.971
...don't go back there,
you leave him alone.


00:43:39.038 --> 00:43:42.303
Both of us... just leave him alone.


00:43:42.375 --> 00:43:44.002
We're done.


00:43:52.752 --> 00:43:54.811
[Angier] I told you, John.


00:43:54.887 --> 00:43:56.980
I don't want you backstage on this one.


00:43:58.624 --> 00:44:01.024
[Angier] I would like to
invite you onstage now


00:44:01.093 --> 00:44:03.789
so that you can examine
the machine for yourselves.


00:44:32.992 --> 00:44:36.723
- Hey, where do you think...?
- I'm part of the bloody act, you fool.


00:44:42.001 --> 00:44:44.196
[electric zapping]


00:44:45.738 --> 00:44:46.727
Who was that?


00:44:50.843 --> 00:44:53.835
[rumbling]


00:45:07.860 --> 00:45:10.351
[zapping continues]


00:45:31.717 --> 00:45:33.309
[silence]


00:45:43.296 --> 00:45:47.426
- [muffled screaming]
- Hey! Where's the bloody key?!


00:45:47.500 --> 00:45:49.058
Where's the bloody key?!


00:45:49.135 --> 00:45:51.433
[Borden yelling]


00:45:51.504 --> 00:45:55.235
Where's the bloody key?!
He's bloody drowning!


00:46:04.483 --> 00:46:05.472
Hold on!


00:46:06.586 --> 00:46:07.610
[screams]


00:46:10.790 --> 00:46:12.257
What have you done?


00:46:34.080 --> 00:46:39.518
[man] Alfred Borden, you have been found
guilty of the murder of Robert Angier.


00:46:39.585 --> 00:46:43.817
You will be hanged
by the neck until dead.


00:46:43.889 --> 00:46:46.858
May the Lord have mercy on your soul.


00:46:48.628 --> 00:46:50.789
[Owens] Mr. Cutter?


00:46:50.863 --> 00:46:52.490
Owens.


00:46:52.565 --> 00:46:55.398
Oh, thank you for coming, Mr. Owens.


00:46:55.468 --> 00:46:59.837
It has fallen to me to dispose
of Mr. Angier's equipment.


00:46:59.905 --> 00:47:01.497
But I notice from this manifest


00:47:01.574 --> 00:47:05.271
that Lord Caldlow has purchased
the bulk of the items.


00:47:05.344 --> 00:47:08.643
Mr. Cutter, if you need to know
where to deliver these items...


00:47:08.714 --> 00:47:12.309
No, it's just there is
one particular item,


00:47:13.252 --> 00:47:15.846
this item, in fact,


00:47:15.921 --> 00:47:18.185
- I would like to...
- You would like to...


00:47:18.257 --> 00:47:19.349
...buy.


00:47:19.425 --> 00:47:21.325
- Buy yourself?
- Yeah, I suppose so.


00:47:22.561 --> 00:47:24.495
- This is the machine?
- Yes.


00:47:24.563 --> 00:47:26.793
Well, I'm afraid
Lord Caldlow was adamant


00:47:26.866 --> 00:47:29.096
about purchasing this particular item.


00:47:29.168 --> 00:47:32.262
Do you think I could
talk to Lord Caldlow in person?


00:47:32.338 --> 00:47:35.102
Out of the question, I'm afraid.


00:47:37.543 --> 00:47:39.443
Of course,


00:47:39.512 --> 00:47:42.743
I suppose if, in the course
of your delivery arrangements,


00:47:42.815 --> 00:47:47.275
your paths were to cross,
I can't stop you speaking your mind.


00:47:48.254 --> 00:47:49.380
Thank you.


00:47:49.522 --> 00:47:50.853
[door opens]


00:47:50.956 --> 00:47:53.117
- [man] Still here, Borden?
- For now.


00:47:53.726 --> 00:47:56.695
You got a visitor. Lord Caldlow.


00:47:56.762 --> 00:47:58.855
With a little girl.


00:48:07.139 --> 00:48:09.039
Jess?


00:48:09.108 --> 00:48:10.735
Hello, my love.


00:48:10.810 --> 00:48:14.268
How are you? I've missed you so much.


00:48:14.346 --> 00:48:16.473
Fallon's missed you too. We both have.


00:48:16.549 --> 00:48:18.881
Daddy, can I come in there?


00:48:19.518 --> 00:48:22.146
Not right now. Not right now, darling.


00:48:22.221 --> 00:48:24.485
No, but everything
is gonna be all right.


00:48:26.058 --> 00:48:27.787
You must be Lord Caldlow?


00:48:27.860 --> 00:48:31.591
Caldlow. Yes, I am. I always have been.


00:48:36.635 --> 00:48:38.830
They flatter you with all those chains.


00:48:38.904 --> 00:48:41.930
Don't they know you can't escape
without your rubber ball?


00:48:42.007 --> 00:48:44.999
I pulled you out... out of that tank.


00:48:45.077 --> 00:48:48.911
All I wanted to do was prove
that I was a better magician.


00:48:48.981 --> 00:48:50.881
But you couldn't leave me alone.


00:48:52.384 --> 00:48:54.477
I don't know what you've done.


00:48:56.388 --> 00:49:00.085
But you're not afraid to get
your hands dirty anymore, are you?


00:49:00.159 --> 00:49:03.424
No, not anymore. And I win.


00:49:03.496 --> 00:49:06.829
No one cares about the man
in the box, the man who disappears.


00:49:06.899 --> 00:49:08.025
You win?


00:49:09.468 --> 00:49:14.132
This ain't a bloody competition
anymore. This is my little girl's life.


00:49:14.206 --> 00:49:17.198
And don't you dare
put her in the middle of this.


00:49:17.276 --> 00:49:20.268
Oh, I know how hard it is
to have someone so special


00:49:20.346 --> 00:49:22.712
taken away from you, don't I, Borden?


00:49:23.716 --> 00:49:26.446
And you can't take it
with you, now, can you?


00:49:26.519 --> 00:49:28.419
Oh, she'll be looked after.


00:49:28.487 --> 00:49:30.512
Goodbye, Professor. Come on, darling.


00:49:30.589 --> 00:49:32.352
No, no, no, no, stop, my darling.


00:49:32.424 --> 00:49:34.551
Look, here.


00:49:36.095 --> 00:49:39.360
That's what you're after.
That's what this is about.


00:49:40.166 --> 00:49:41.531
Take it.


00:49:41.600 --> 00:49:43.295
- Your secret?
- Yeah.


00:49:46.505 --> 00:49:50.066
You always were the better magician.
We both know that.


00:49:50.709 --> 00:49:53.303
Whatever your secret was,
you have to agree,


00:49:54.446 --> 00:49:55.777
mine is better.


00:49:57.483 --> 00:50:00.850
Don't do this. Don't do this,
Angier. Jess, Jess!


00:50:00.920 --> 00:50:04.447
Jess, I'm gonna take you
home soon. I promise.


00:50:04.523 --> 00:50:07.083
- For God's sake.
- I promise. Look!


00:50:10.930 --> 00:50:14.525
I promise. I love you, Jess.


00:50:14.600 --> 00:50:16.261
I love you.


00:50:16.335 --> 00:50:17.962
- Come on.
- I love you.


00:50:18.037 --> 00:50:19.732
I love you, Jess.


00:50:19.805 --> 00:50:22.137
Angier! Angier!


00:50:22.208 --> 00:50:24.301
What, do you think
this place can hold me?


00:50:24.376 --> 00:50:27.402
Angier! They're gonna bloody hang me!


00:50:27.479 --> 00:50:30.004
And you can put a stop to this now!


00:50:30.649 --> 00:50:32.844
Listen! Listen! That man...


00:50:32.918 --> 00:50:35.284
Listen, that man is
the one I'm in for killing!


00:50:35.354 --> 00:50:39.688
Listen! If he's alive, I'm not guilty!


00:50:39.758 --> 00:50:42.022
- I'm not guilty!
- I don't care!


00:50:42.094 --> 00:50:44.187
- Get hold of him.
- Angier!


00:50:48.868 --> 00:50:51.428
Run along now.


00:50:51.503 --> 00:50:54.028
Sir, there's a gentleman waiting.


00:51:10.856 --> 00:51:13.586
- Dear God.
- Hello, Cutter.


00:51:14.560 --> 00:51:16.994
You're still alive.


00:51:17.062 --> 00:51:18.927
How is it you're still alive?


00:51:18.998 --> 00:51:21.398
I saw you on a slab, for God's sake.


00:51:24.403 --> 00:51:26.428
- Child.
- Good night, sir.


00:51:26.505 --> 00:51:28.473
[Angier] Good night, Jess.


00:51:29.708 --> 00:51:31.369
I've seen her before.


00:51:31.443 --> 00:51:33.968
I saw her in court with...


00:51:34.914 --> 00:51:36.541
...Fallon.


00:51:38.651 --> 00:51:41.245
- What have you done?
- She needs looking after.


00:51:41.320 --> 00:51:43.811
She needs her father.


00:51:43.889 --> 00:51:46.858
You're letting him hang,
and I helped you.


00:51:46.926 --> 00:51:51.863
I came here to beg Lord Caldlow
to let me destroy that machine.


00:51:53.332 --> 00:51:56.768
I am not going to beg you for anything.


00:51:56.835 --> 00:52:00.100
You don't have to. I'm gonna
make sure it is never used again.


00:52:01.240 --> 00:52:04.334
Then, Lord Caldlow...


00:52:06.879 --> 00:52:08.938
...where do you want me to deliver it?


00:52:09.014 --> 00:52:12.780
My theater. It belongs
with the prestige materials.


00:52:13.252 --> 00:52:15.846
John, I tried not to involve you.


00:52:28.801 --> 00:52:31.065
So...


00:52:33.105 --> 00:52:35.699
We go alone now.


00:52:35.774 --> 00:52:38.208
Both of us.


00:52:41.013 --> 00:52:44.414
I mean, I don't have
as far to go as you.


00:52:49.722 --> 00:52:51.053
No.


00:52:52.591 --> 00:52:55.651
You were right. I should have
left him to his damn trick.


00:52:57.429 --> 00:52:59.522
I'm sorry.


00:53:01.066 --> 00:53:03.398
I'm sorry for a lot of things.


00:53:04.536 --> 00:53:07.266
I'm sorry about Sarah.


00:53:08.374 --> 00:53:11.832
Didn't mean to hurt her, I didn't.


00:53:13.712 --> 00:53:18.046
You go live your life in full now,
all right? You live for both of us.


00:53:26.892 --> 00:53:28.382
Goodbye.


00:54:14.173 --> 00:54:16.607
Are you watching closely?


00:54:47.973 --> 00:54:49.907
Put it down on the end.


00:55:23.308 --> 00:55:27.074
Take a minute to consider
your achievement.


00:55:28.147 --> 00:55:30.945
I once told you about a sailor


00:55:31.016 --> 00:55:33.314
who described drowning to me.


00:55:33.385 --> 00:55:35.580
Yes, he said it was like going home.


00:55:36.688 --> 00:55:40.454
I was lying. He said it was agony.


00:56:20.199 --> 00:56:24.363
[man] Alfred Borden, this day,
in the name of the king


00:56:24.436 --> 00:56:26.427
and the High Court of England,


00:56:26.505 --> 00:56:28.336
you will meet your end.


00:56:30.442 --> 00:56:32.467
No one cares about the man in the box.


00:56:37.316 --> 00:56:39.045
Cutter?


00:56:43.722 --> 00:56:45.246
Cutter!


00:56:47.125 --> 00:56:49.389
[man] Do you have anything to say?


00:56:54.132 --> 00:56:55.531
Abracadabra.


00:57:01.707 --> 00:57:03.265
[gunshot]


00:57:07.012 --> 00:57:09.276
[moans]


00:57:19.258 --> 00:57:22.284
[Angier moans]


00:57:32.170 --> 00:57:34.900
A brother? A twin?


00:57:36.742 --> 00:57:39.108
You were Fallon.


00:57:40.612 --> 00:57:43.274
- The whole time?
- No.


00:57:44.316 --> 00:57:46.648
We were both Fallon.


00:57:46.718 --> 00:57:48.618
We were both Borden.


00:57:53.992 --> 00:57:56.961
Were you the one who went into the box?


00:57:57.029 --> 00:57:58.724
Or the one who came back out?


00:58:00.032 --> 00:58:02.330
We took turns.


00:58:07.139 --> 00:58:09.198
The trick is where we would swap.


00:58:15.414 --> 00:58:17.314
Cutter knew. Cutter knew.


00:58:17.382 --> 00:58:19.646
But I told him it was
too simple, too easy.


00:58:20.852 --> 00:58:21.841
No.


00:58:23.388 --> 00:58:25.356
Simple, maybe, but not easy.


00:58:25.424 --> 00:58:29.190
There's nothing easy
about two men sharing one life.


00:58:34.866 --> 00:58:38.063
I don't understand,
how it can be bleeding again?


00:58:41.540 --> 00:58:44.338
Wha... What about Olivia and your wife?


00:58:45.344 --> 00:58:47.244
We each loved one of them.


00:58:50.882 --> 00:58:53.612
I loved Sarah.


00:58:53.685 --> 00:58:56.210
He loved Olivia.


00:58:56.288 --> 00:58:58.722
We each had half of a full life,


00:58:58.790 --> 00:59:01.782
really, which was enough for us...


00:59:01.860 --> 00:59:02.849
...just.


00:59:05.497 --> 00:59:07.226
But not for them.


00:59:09.801 --> 00:59:12.031
See, sacrifice, Robert,


00:59:12.104 --> 00:59:14.834
that's the price of a good trick.


00:59:16.875 --> 00:59:19.435
You wouldn't know
anything about that, would you?


00:59:19.511 --> 00:59:22.639
[groaning]


00:59:22.714 --> 00:59:24.648
I've... I've made sacrifices.


00:59:24.716 --> 00:59:26.684
- No.
- Yes.


00:59:27.152 --> 00:59:30.246
It takes nothing
to steal another man's work.


00:59:30.322 --> 00:59:33.086
Yeah, it takes everything.


00:59:53.145 --> 00:59:55.272
No, no, wait, I'm not...


00:59:55.347 --> 00:59:57.008
[gunshot]


01:00:01.953 --> 01:00:04.581
It took courage.


01:00:06.591 --> 01:00:09.788
It took courage to climb
into that machine every night,


01:00:10.595 --> 01:00:13.029
not knowing...


01:00:13.098 --> 01:00:15.225
...if I'd be the man in the box...


01:00:18.270 --> 01:00:19.532
...or in the prestige.


01:00:20.872 --> 01:00:23.898
Do you want to see...


01:00:23.975 --> 01:00:26.273
...what it cost me?


01:00:26.344 --> 01:00:29.108
You didn't see where you are, did you?


01:00:30.015 --> 01:00:32.415
Look. Look.


01:00:33.518 --> 01:00:35.008
I don't care.


01:00:39.724 --> 01:00:43.285
You went halfway around the world.


01:00:43.361 --> 01:00:46.125
You spent a fortune.


01:00:48.200 --> 01:00:50.725
You did terrible things.


01:00:51.736 --> 01:00:54.204
Really terrible things, Robert.


01:00:56.241 --> 01:00:57.731
And all for nothing.


01:00:58.710 --> 01:00:59.904
For nothing?


01:00:59.978 --> 01:01:01.309
[Borden] Yeah.


01:01:04.983 --> 01:01:07.611
You never understood...


01:01:07.686 --> 01:01:09.677
...why we did this.


01:01:12.791 --> 01:01:15.351
The audience knows the truth.


01:01:16.495 --> 01:01:18.929
The world is simple.


01:01:18.997 --> 01:01:20.726
It's miserable.


01:01:20.799 --> 01:01:24.496
Solid... Solid all the way through.


01:01:26.838 --> 01:01:29.170
But if you could fool them,


01:01:29.241 --> 01:01:31.402
even for a second...


01:01:32.944 --> 01:01:35.344
...then you could make them wonder.


01:01:36.481 --> 01:01:38.676
And then you...


01:01:38.750 --> 01:01:40.980
Then you got to see something


01:01:41.052 --> 01:01:42.713
very special.


01:01:47.025 --> 01:01:49.550
You really don't know.


01:01:52.631 --> 01:01:54.292
It was...


01:01:55.367 --> 01:01:58.336
...it was the look on their faces.


01:02:01.273 --> 01:02:03.070
[inhales deeply]


01:02:13.518 --> 01:02:18.353
<i>[Cutter] Every magic trick</i>
<i>consists of three parts, or acts.</i>


01:02:21.793 --> 01:02:25.251
<i>The first part is called "the pledge."</i>


01:02:25.330 --> 01:02:28.094
<i>The magician shows you</i>
<i>something ordinary.</i>


01:02:29.234 --> 01:02:32.169
<i>The second act is called "the turn."</i>


01:02:33.638 --> 01:02:36.505
<i>The magician takes</i>
<i>the ordinary something</i>


01:02:36.575 --> 01:02:39.442
<i>and makes it into</i>
<i>something extraordinary.</i>


01:02:40.779 --> 01:02:44.681
<i>But you wouldn't clap yet,</i>
<i>because making something disappear</i>


01:02:44.749 --> 01:02:48.845
<i>isn't enough. You have to bring it back.</i>


01:03:23.288 --> 01:03:25.722
<i>Now you're looking for the secret.</i>


01:03:28.660 --> 01:03:32.391
<i>But you won't find it, because,</i>
<i>of course, you're not really looking.</i>


01:03:35.500 --> 01:03:38.936
<i>You don't really want to work it out.</i>


01:03:41.740 --> 01:03:44.038
<i>You want to be fooled.</i>

